          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Change Summary Generation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJE_LLM_CHANGE_SUMMARY_GENERATION",
          "id": "1770636275945",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770636275947_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### References\nBasic information about the Change order is given below in json format:\n{\n\"\"BasicDetails\"\" : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.changeOrderSummary}} ,\n\"\"ImpactNames\"\" :  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.impactNames}},\n\"\"ImpactDescriptions\"\" : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.impactDescriptions}} ,\n\"\"ImpactDetails\"\" : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.impactDetails}} \n}\n\nThe most affected phases or deliverables are given below in json format:\n{\n \"\"Phases\"\" : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.tasks}} ,\n \"\"Deliverables\"\": {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.deliverables}} \n}\n\n### Instructions\nYou are an experienced Project Manager with expertise in change management and writing succinct summaries to communicate the same to executive stakeholders. Your current assignment involves drafting a summary of a change order, drawing on the provided References. If the information provided contains information not relevant or is inappropriate for workplace, ignore the information while generating the response.\nMake sure to respond in the following language only: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJE_TOOL_GET_USER_LANGUAGE.$output[0].Language}}\n\n\n### Structure and Content\nProvide the response in a RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format:\n{\n\"\"first_paragraph\"\" : \"\"<< Include text based on the BasicDetails of the change order. This 100 word long paragraph summarizes the BasicDetails of the change order without getting to the details about the amounts and impacted phases. Talk only about the given details.>>\"\",\n\"\"second_paragraph\"\" : \"\"<< Do not generate this paragraph at all if there is no information provided. Include text based on ImpactDetails of the change order. If ImpactDetails is blank, this section should be blank.  Else, this 100 word long paragraph should convey the impact to the project. Talk only about the given details. Do not generate this paragraph at all if there is no information provided.>>\"\",\n\"\"third_paragraph\"\":\"\"<< If both Phases and Deliverables are null, keep the paragraph blank. Only generate this paragraph if there is information provided for most affected phases in Phases and Deliverables. Include text based on Phases and Deliverables of the change order. This 50 word long paragraph should convey the impact on the scope for the project. Talk only about the given details.>>\"\"\n}\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Use simple, clear, professional, and naturally flowing language, keeping the narrative in third person and maintaining a neutral tone. The summary should be precise, avoiding any formal closures, or signatures.\n- Use the exact capitalization for Phases and Deliverables as provided, but do not add quotes or special characters.\n- Make sure to directly copy the value and currency from the input and maintain usage of commas/spaces while removing currency symbols like the dollar sign.\n- Strictly do not talk about information that is not provided.\n- Do not speculate the consequences of the impacts on the project.\n- Do not explain the actions to be taken or the aim of the change order.\n- Any impacts on the change order will not be incorporated in the project until it is implemented at the end, do not mention about incorporation of the change order.\n- Strictly restate only the information explicitly provided in the input. Do not infer, interpret, or expand meaning.\n- Do not include intent, purpose, expected outcomes, benefits, or implications unless explicitly stated.\n- Do not add explanatory or contextual language such as \"aims to\", \"seeks to\", \"is intended to\", \"helps\", \"supports\", \"enhances\", \"drives\", or similar phrases.\n- Do not introduce any new words or concepts that are not directly traceable to the input.\n- If a sentence cannot be formed without adding new meaning, omit that sentence.\n- Do not add operational, procedural, or implementation details such as integration, training, configuration, workflows, coordination, monitoring, tracking, reporting, or execution unless explicitly stated in the input.\n- Do not include stakeholder expectations, assumptions, or organizational context unless explicitly provided.\n- Do not mention timelines, compliance, or team coordination unless explicitly present in the input.\n- Do not expand financial details beyond the exact values given. Do not explain how costs, revenue, or contract values are used.\n- Keep each sentence directly traceable to the input. Remove any sentence that cannot be mapped back to the input content.\n- If a financial amount is already mentioned, do not mention it again in the same paragraph.\n- Do not describe the same impact using multiple sentences.\n- Do not add redundant sentences to meet word count. It is acceptable to be shorter if repetition would occur.\n\n### Disallowed Content\nThe response must NOT include:\n- Repetition of content\n- stakeholder expectations\n- coordination between teams\n- implementation steps (integration, training, configuration)\n- financial breakdowns or usage explanations\n- monitoring, tracking, reporting, execution details\n- timeline statements unless explicitly provided\n\n### Final Check\n- One or multiple paragraph values can be blank, and each must be handled independently. Failure to comply with this requirement could result in critical issues. For example, just the second paragraph could be blank.\n- Do not repeat information across paragraphs. Keep each paragraph concise.\n- If amounts are present in the output, it should be formatted appropriately such as 1200.40 USD, with the value first followed by currency code. Remove all currency symbols like the dollar sign unless they appear in the input.\n- Ensure all cost values are formatted with the correct number of decimal places based on the currency code (e.g., USD/EUR = 2 decimals, JPY = 0 decimals, KWD = 3 decimals).\n- Only when the terms \"budget\" or \"forecast\" are used in the impact details parameter input, explicitly use them in the output. Do not use the terms \"budget\" or \"forecast\" otherwise.\n- Strictly avoid phrases including but not limited to \"\"There is no information\"\" \"\"justified by\"\", \"\"justification for this\"\", \"\"specifically targeting\"\", \"\"the summary\"\", \"\"the first paragraph\"\", \"\"no information\"\", \"\"not specified\"\", \"\"no specific\"\", \"\"no deliverables specified\"\", \"\"no information provided\"\", \"\"no other\"\", \"\"no further detail\"\".\n- Do not hallucinate or talk about information that is not provided, only talk about what is given in the input, avoid repetition.\n- Ensure the response is strictly valid JSON, free of additional characters like </code>, symbols, or formatting issues that would invalidate the JSON."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
